# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.js
.yarn/install-state.gz

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
# Throwaway build dirs from PULSEBLR_DIST_DIR — see the note on `distDir` in next.config.ts.
# `/.next/` does NOT cover these: it is an exact directory name, not a prefix.
/.next-*/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# local env files
.env*.local
.env.local
.env.development.local
.env.test.local
.env.production.local

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# playwright
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/blob-report/
/playwright/.cache/

# IDE
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
Thumbs.db

# Made with Bob

# Local tooling output
lint-out.txt
lint2.txt

# Claude Code local launch config (machine-specific ports/commands)
.claude/launch.json

# Security-scan working directories
CLAUDE-SECURITY-*/

# Debug and probe artefacts. These are generated locally and have been observed to
# contain real credentials -- the Playwright console logs captured a Google API key and
# digest_probe.json captured passwords in URL params -- so they must never be staged.
.playwright-mcp/
digest_probe.json
*.log
audit-report.md
COMMIT_MSG.txt
PR_BODY.md

# gstack skill working directory: QA reports, screenshots and baselines. Local tool
# output like the entries above, and the screenshots can be large.
.gstack/

# Competitor research and product idea notes. Working documents, not repo documentation:
# they describe someone else's site and our unbuilt plans, both of which go stale fast.
# Anything from them that turns out to be load-bearing belongs in CLAUDE.md instead, which
# is why no committed file may cite these by name.
HEAPHEAPHURRAY-AUDIT.md
IMPROVEMENT-IDEAS.md

# Audit working notes: live corpus diagnostics, agent reports and raw upstream captures.
# Local tool output like the entries above — measurements go stale, and the diag captures
# include upstream response bodies. Load-bearing conclusions belong in CLAUDE.md instead.
/audit/

# Isolated verify builds from scripts/start-verify.js, and the layout harness a stream used to
# hit-test tap targets. Both machine-local: a second dev server needs its own distDir so it does
# not swap the route manifest under a session already using `.next`, which produces phantom 404s
# on routes that exist.
.next-verify*/
_layout-harness/

# Android signing keys, added ahead of the Play Store TWA build.
# Committing one hands anyone the ability to ship an update as you; LOSING one means you can
# never update the app again, because Play matches uploads on the signing key. Back the keystore
# up somewhere outside this repo before the first `bubblewrap build`.
*.keystore
*.jks

# The Bubblewrap-generated Android project is DERIVED from twa-manifest.json, which is the only
# part worth committing — Bubblewrap's own docs say manual edits to the project are overwritten
# on `update`. Note the pattern excludes CONTENTS (`/android/*`) rather than the directory:
# git does not descend into an excluded directory, so `/android/` would make the negation below
# silently ineffective and the one file you needed would be the one that vanished.
/android/*
!/android/twa-manifest.json
